#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Guide for the configuration of an LDAP server for authentication on FreeBSD"
msgstr "FreeBSD 上用于身份验证的 LDAP 服务器配置指南"

#. type: Title =
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:1
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:12
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "LDAP Authentication"
msgstr "LDAP 身份验证"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:44
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr "摘要"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:47
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This document is intended as a guide for the configuration of an LDAP server "
"(principally an OpenLDAP server) for authentication on FreeBSD.  This is "
"useful for situations where many servers need the same user accounts, for "
"example as a replacement for NIS."
msgstr "本文旨在指导如何配置 LDAP 服务器（主要是 OpenLDAP 服务器），以便在 FreeBSD 上进行身份验证。在许多服务器需要使用相同用户帐户的情况下，这很有用，例如替代 NIS。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:49
msgid "'''"
msgstr "'''"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preface"
msgstr "前言"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:57
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This document is intended to give the reader enough of an understanding of "
"LDAP to configure an LDAP server.  This document will attempt to provide an "
"explanation of package:net/nss_ldap[] and package:security/pam_ldap[] for "
"use with client machines services for use with the LDAP server."
msgstr "本文旨在帮助读者充分理解 LDAP，以便配置 LDAP 服务器。本文将介绍如何使用 package:net/nss_ldap[] 和 package:security/pam_ldap[]，使客户端计算机上的服务能够与 LDAP 服务器配合使用。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:59
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When finished, the reader should be able to configure and deploy a FreeBSD "
"server that can host an LDAP directory, and to configure and deploy a "
"FreeBSD server which can authenticate against an LDAP directory."
msgstr "阅读本文后，读者应能够配置和部署一台可托管 LDAP 目录的 FreeBSD 服务器，并配置和部署一台可通过 LDAP 目录进行身份验证的 FreeBSD 服务器。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:63
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This article is not intended to be an exhaustive account of the security, "
"robustness, or best practice considerations for configuring LDAP or the "
"other services discussed herein.  While the author takes care to do "
"everything correctly, they do not address security issues beyond a general "
"scope.  This article should be considered to lay the theoretical groundwork "
"only, and any actual implementation should be accompanied by careful "
"requirement analysis."
msgstr "本文并非旨在全面介绍配置 LDAP 或本文所讨论的其他服务时涉及的安全性、健壮性或最佳实践方面的考量。尽管作者尽力确保所有操作正确，但本文不会讨论一般范围以外的安全问题。本文仅应视为理论基础；任何实际部署都应经过仔细的需求分析。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:65
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Configuring LDAP"
msgstr "配置 LDAP"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:70
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"LDAP stands for \"Lightweight Directory Access Protocol\" and is a subset of "
"the X.500 Directory Access Protocol.  Its most recent specifications are in "
"http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc4510.txt[RFC4510] and friends.  Essentially it is "
"a database that expects to be read from more often than it is written to."
msgstr "LDAP 是“轻量级目录访问协议”（Lightweight Directory Access Protocol）的缩写，是 X.500 目录访问协议的一个子集。其最新规范见 link:http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc4510.txt[RFC4510] 及相关文档。从本质上说，它是一种读取频率高于写入频率的数据库。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:74
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The LDAP server http://www.openldap.org/[OpenLDAP] will be used in the "
"examples in this document; while the principles here should be generally "
"applicable to many different servers, most of the concrete administration is "
"OpenLDAP-specific.  There are several server versions in ports, for example "
"package:net/openldap26-server[].  Client servers will need the corresponding "
"package:net/openldap26-client[] libraries."
msgstr "本文示例将使用 LDAP 服务器 link:http://www.openldap.org/[OpenLDAP]；虽然这里介绍的原则通常适用于许多不同的服务器，但大多数具体管理操作都针对 OpenLDAP。ports 中有多个服务器版本，例如 package:net/openldap26-server[]。客户端服务器需要安装相应的 package:net/openldap26-client[] 库。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:77
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There are (basically) two areas of the LDAP service which need "
"configuration.  The first is setting up a server to receive connections "
"properly, and the second is adding entries to the server's directory so that "
"FreeBSD tools know how to interact with it."
msgstr "LDAP 服务基本上有两个方面需要配置。首先是设置服务器以正确接收连接；其次是向服务器目录添加条目，以便 FreeBSD 工具知道如何与其交互。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:79
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Setting Up the Server for Connections"
msgstr "设置服务器以接收连接"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:85
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This section is specific to OpenLDAP.  If you are using another server, you "
"will need to consult that server's documentation."
msgstr "本节内容仅适用于 OpenLDAP。如果使用其他服务器，请参阅该服务器的文档。"

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:88
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:93
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Installing OpenLDAP"
msgstr "安装 OpenLDAP"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:91
#, fuzzy
msgid "First, install OpenLDAP:"
msgstr "首先，安装 OpenLDAP："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:101
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/ports/net/openldap26-server\n"
"# make install clean\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/ports/net/openldap26-server\n# make install clean\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:106
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This installs the `slapd` and `slurpd` binaries, along with the required "
"OpenLDAP libraries."
msgstr "这将安装 `slapd` 和 `slurpd` 二进制文件，以及所需的 OpenLDAP 库。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:108
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Configuring OpenLDAP"
msgstr "配置 OpenLDAP"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:111
#, fuzzy
msgid "Next we must configure OpenLDAP."
msgstr "接下来，我们必须配置 OpenLDAP。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:114
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You will want to require encryption in your connections to the LDAP server; "
"otherwise your users' passwords will be transferred in plain text, which is "
"considered insecure.  The tools we will be using support two very similar "
"kinds of encryption, SSL and TLS."
msgstr "建议要求与 LDAP 服务器之间的连接使用加密；否则，用户密码将以明文传输，这被认为是不安全的。我们将使用的工具支持两种非常相似的加密方式：SSL 和 TLS。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:117
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"TLS stands for \"Transportation Layer Security\".  Services that employ TLS "
"tend to connect on the _same_ ports as the same services without TLS; thus "
"an SMTP server which supports TLS will listen for connections on port 25, "
"and an LDAP server will listen on 389."
msgstr "TLS 是“传输层安全”（Transportation Layer Security）的缩写。使用 TLS 的服务通常与未使用 TLS 的同类服务监听相同端口；因此，支持 TLS 的 SMTP 服务器会在端口 25 上监听连接，LDAP 服务器则会在端口 389 上监听。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:120
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"SSL stands for \"Secure Sockets Layer\", and services that implement SSL do "
"_not_ listen on the same ports as their non-SSL counterparts.  Thus SMTPS "
"listens on port 465 (not 25), HTTPS listens on 443, and LDAPS on 636."
msgstr "SSL 是“安全套接字层”（Secure Sockets Layer）的缩写。实现 SSL 的服务__不会__监听与非 SSL 服务相同的端口。因此，SMTPS 监听端口 465（而不是 25），HTTPS 监听端口 443，LDAPS 监听端口 636。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:124
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The reason SSL uses a different port than TLS is because a TLS connection "
"begins as plain text, and switches to encrypted traffic after the `STARTTLS` "
"directive.  SSL connections are encrypted from the beginning.  Other than "
"that there are no substantial differences between the two."
msgstr "SSL 使用与 TLS 不同端口的原因是，TLS 连接以明文开始，并在收到 `STARTTLS` 指令后切换为加密通信。SSL 连接从一开始就经过加密。除此之外，两者没有显著差异。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:128
#, fuzzy
msgid "We will adjust OpenLDAP to use TLS, as SSL is considered deprecated."
msgstr "我们将调整 OpenLDAP 以使用 TLS，因为 SSL 已被视为弃用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:131
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once OpenLDAP is installed via ports, the following configuration parameters "
"in [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/openldap/slapd.conf# will enable TLS:"
msgstr "通过 ports 安装 OpenLDAP 后，在 [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/openldap/slapd.conf# 中设置以下配置参数即可启用 TLS："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:135
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "security ssf=128\n"
msgstr "security ssf=128\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:139
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"TLSCertificateFile /path/to/your/cert.crt\n"
"TLSCertificateKeyFile /path/to/your/cert.key\n"
"TLSCACertificateFile /path/to/your/cacert.crt\n"
msgstr "TLSCertificateFile /path/to/your/cert.crt\nTLSCertificateKeyFile /path/to/your/cert.key\nTLSCACertificateFile /path/to/your/cacert.crt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:143
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Here, `ssf=128` tells OpenLDAP to require 128-bit encryption for all "
"connections, both search and update.  This parameter may be configured based "
"on the security needs of your site, but rarely you need to weaken it, as "
"most LDAP client libraries support strong encryption."
msgstr "此处的 `ssf=128` 告诉 OpenLDAP，所有连接（包括搜索和更新）都必须使用 128 位加密。可根据站点的安全需求配置此参数，但通常很少需要降低要求，因为大多数 LDAP 客户端库都支持强加密。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:146
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The [.filename]#cert.crt#, [.filename]#cert.key#, and [.filename]#cacert."
"crt# files are necessary for clients to authenticate _you_ as the valid LDAP "
"server.  If you simply want a server that runs, you can create a self-signed "
"certificate with OpenSSL:"
msgstr "客户端需要使用 [.filename]#cert.crt#、[.filename]#cert.key# 和 [.filename]#cacert.crt# 文件来验证__你__确实是有效的 LDAP 服务器。如果只想让服务器运行起来，可以使用 OpenSSL 创建自签名证书："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:148
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Generating an RSA Key"
msgstr "生成 RSA 密钥"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:159
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% openssl genrsa -out cert.key 1024\n"
"Generating RSA private key, 1024 bit long modulus\n"
"....................++++++\n"
"...++++++\n"
"e is 65537 (0x10001)\n"
msgstr "% openssl genrsa -out cert.key 1024\nGenerating RSA private key, 1024 bit long modulus\n....................++++++\n...++++++\ne is 65537 (0x10001)\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:161
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% openssl req -new -key cert.key -out cert.csr\n"
msgstr "% openssl req -new -key cert.key -out cert.csr\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:170
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"At this point you should be prompted for some values.  You may enter "
"whatever values you like; however, it is important the \"Common Name\" value "
"be the fully qualified domain name of the OpenLDAP server.  In our case, and "
"the examples here, the server is _server.example.org_.  Incorrectly setting "
"this value will cause clients to fail when making connections.  This can the "
"cause of great frustration, so ensure that you follow these steps closely."
msgstr "此时系统会提示输入一些值。可以输入任意值；但“Common Name”值必须是 OpenLDAP 服务器的完全限定域名。在本例及本文的示例中，服务器名为 _server.example.org_。如果此值设置不正确，客户端连接将失败。这可能令人非常沮丧，因此请务必严格按照这些步骤操作。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:172
#, fuzzy
msgid "Finally, the certificate signing request needs to be signed:"
msgstr "最后，需要对证书签名请求进行签名："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:174
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Self-signing the Certificate"
msgstr "自签名证书"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:184
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% openssl x509 -req -in cert.csr -days 365 -signkey cert.key -out cert.crt\n"
"Signature ok\n"
"subject=/C=AU/ST=Some-State/O=Internet Widgits Pty Ltd\n"
"Getting Private key\n"
msgstr "% openssl x509 -req -in cert.csr -days 365 -signkey cert.key -out cert.crt\nSignature ok\nsubject=/C=AU/ST=Some-State/O=Internet Widgits Pty Ltd\nGetting Private key\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:191
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This will create a self-signed certificate that can be used for the "
"directives in [.filename]#slapd.conf#, where [.filename]#cert.crt# and [."
"filename]#cacert.crt# are the same file.  If you are going to use many "
"OpenLDAP servers (for replication via `slurpd`) you will want to see "
"crossref:ldap-auth[ssl-ca, OpenSSL Certificates for LDAP] to generate a CA "
"key and use it to sign individual server certificates."
msgstr "这将创建一个自签名证书，可用于 [.filename]#slapd.conf# 中的指令，其中 [.filename]#cert.crt# 和 [.filename]#cacert.crt# 是同一个文件。如果要使用多台 OpenLDAP 服务器（通过 `slurpd` 进行复制），请参阅 crossref:ldap-auth[ssl-ca, OpenSSL Certificates for LDAP]，以生成 CA 密钥并用其为各个服务器证书签名。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:193
#, fuzzy
msgid "Once this is done, put the following in [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#:"
msgstr "完成后，将以下内容添加到 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:197
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "slapd_enable=\"YES\"\n"
msgstr "slapd_enable=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:202
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then run `/usr/local/etc/rc.d/slapd start`.  This should start OpenLDAP.  "
"Confirm that it is listening on 389 with"
msgstr "然后运行 `/usr/local/etc/rc.d/slapd start`。这应该会启动 OpenLDAP。使用以下命令确认它正在端口 389 上监听："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:207
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% sockstat -4 -p 389\n"
"ldap     slapd      3261  7  tcp4   *:389                 *:*\n"
msgstr "% sockstat -4 -p 389\nldap     slapd      3261  7  tcp4   *:389                 *:*\n"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:210
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring the Client"
msgstr "设定客户端"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:214
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Install the package:net/openldap26-client[] port for the OpenLDAP "
"libraries.  The client machines will always have OpenLDAP libraries since "
"that is all package:security/pam_ldap[] and package:net/nss_ldap[] support, "
"at least for the moment."
msgstr "安装 package:net/openldap26-client[] port 以获取 OpenLDAP 库。客户端计算机始终需要 OpenLDAP 库，因为至少目前 package:security/pam_ldap[] 和 package:net/nss_ldap[] 只支持这些库。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:217
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The configuration file for the OpenLDAP libraries is [.filename]#/usr/local/"
"etc/openldap/ldap.conf#.  Edit this file to contain the following values:"
msgstr "OpenLDAP 库的配置文件是 [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/openldap/ldap.conf#。编辑此文件并填入以下值："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:224
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"base dc=example,dc=org\n"
"uri ldap://server.example.org/\n"
"ssl start_tls\n"
"tls_cacert /path/to/your/cacert.crt\n"
msgstr "base dc=example,dc=org\nuri ldap://server.example.org/\nssl start_tls\ntls_cacert /path/to/your/cacert.crt\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:229
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It is important that your clients have access to [.filename]#cacert.crt#, "
"otherwise they will not be able to connect."
msgstr "客户端必须能够访问 [.filename]#cacert.crt#，否则将无法连接。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:236
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There are two files called [.filename]#ldap.conf#.  The first is this file, "
"which is for the OpenLDAP libraries and defines how to talk to the server.  "
"The second is [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/ldap.conf#, and is for pam_ldap."
msgstr "有两个名为 [.filename]#ldap.conf# 的文件。第一个是此文件，供 OpenLDAP 库使用，用于定义如何与服务器通信。第二个是 [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/ldap.conf#，供 pam_ldap 使用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:241
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"At this point you should be able to run `ldapsearch -Z` on the client "
"machine; `-Z` means \"use TLS\".  If you encounter an error, then something "
"is configured wrong; most likely it is your certificates.  Use man:"
"openssl[1]'s `s_client` and `s_server` to ensure you have them configured "
"and signed properly."
msgstr "此时，应该可以在客户端计算机上运行 `ldapsearch -Z`；`-Z` 表示“使用 TLS”。如果遇到错误，则说明某些配置有误，最可能是证书配置问题。使用 man:openssl[1] 的 `s_client` 和 `s_server` 确认证书配置和签名正确。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:243
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Entries in the Database"
msgstr "数据库中的条目"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:248
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Authentication against an LDAP directory is generally accomplished by "
"attempting to bind to the directory as the connecting user.  This is done by "
"establishing a \"simple\" bind on the directory with the user name "
"supplied.  If there is an entry with the `uid` equal to the user name and "
"that entry's `userPassword` attribute matches the password supplied, then "
"the bind is successful."
msgstr "通常，通过 LDAP 目录进行身份验证的方式是尝试以连接用户的身份绑定到目录。这是通过使用提供的用户名对目录执行“simple”绑定来完成的。如果存在一条 `uid` 与用户名相同，且该条目的 `userPassword` 属性与提供的密码匹配的记录，则绑定成功。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:250
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first thing we have to do is figure out is where in the directory our "
"users will live."
msgstr "首先要确定用户将存放在目录中的哪个位置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:254
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The base entry for our database is `dc=example,dc=org`.  The default "
"location for users that most clients seem to expect is something like "
"`ou=people,_base_`, so that is what will be used here.  However keep in mind "
"that this is configurable."
msgstr "数据库的基本条目为 `dc=example,dc=org`。大多数客户端所期望的用户默认位置类似于 `ou=people,_base_`，因此本例将使用该位置。但请记住，此项可以配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:256
#, fuzzy
msgid "So the ldif entry for the `people` organizational unit will look like:"
msgstr "因此，`people` 组织单位的 ldif 条目如下所示："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:263
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dn: ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"
"objectClass: top\n"
"objectClass: organizationalUnit\n"
"ou: people\n"
msgstr "dn: ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\nobjectClass: top\nobjectClass: organizationalUnit\nou: people\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:266
#, fuzzy
msgid "All users will be created as subentries of this organizational unit."
msgstr "所有用户都将作为此组织单位的子条目创建。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:271
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Some thought might be given to the object class your users will belong to.  "
"Most tools by default will use `people`, which is fine if you simply want to "
"provide entries against which to authenticate.  However, if you are going to "
"store user information in the LDAP database as well, you will probably want "
"to use `inetOrgPerson`, which has many useful attributes.  In either case, "
"the relevant schemas need to be loaded in [.filename]#slapd.conf#."
msgstr "可以考虑用户所属的对象类。大多数工具默认使用 `people`；如果只需要提供用于身份验证的条目，这就足够了。但是，如果还要在 LDAP 数据库中存储用户信息，通常应使用 `inetOrgPerson`，它包含许多有用的属性。无论使用哪种对象类，都需要在 [.filename]#slapd.conf# 中加载相应的 schema。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:274
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For this example we will use the `person` object class.  If you are using "
"`inetOrgPerson`, the steps are basically identical, except that the `sn` "
"attribute is required."
msgstr "本例将使用 `person` 对象类。如果使用 `inetOrgPerson`，步骤基本相同，但必须提供 `sn` 属性。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:276
#, fuzzy
msgid "To add a test-user named `tuser`, the ldif would be:"
msgstr "要添加名为 `tuser` 的测试用户，ldif 内容如下："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:290
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dn: uid=tuser,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"
"objectClass: person\n"
"objectClass: posixAccount\n"
"objectClass: shadowAccount\n"
"objectClass: top\n"
"uidNumber: 10000\n"
"gidNumber: 10000\n"
"homeDirectory: /home/tuser\n"
"loginShell: /bin/csh\n"
"uid: tuser\n"
"cn: tuser\n"
msgstr "dn: uid=tuser,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\nobjectClass: person\nobjectClass: posixAccount\nobjectClass: shadowAccount\nobjectClass: top\nuidNumber: 10000\ngidNumber: 10000\nhomeDirectory: /home/tuser\nloginShell: /bin/csh\nuid: tuser\ncn: tuser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:293
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I start my LDAP users' UIDs at 10000 to avoid collisions with system "
"accounts; you can configure whatever number you wish here, as long as it is "
"less than 65536."
msgstr "我将 LDAP 用户的 UID 从 10000 开始分配，以避免与系统帐户冲突；这里可以配置为任意数字，但必须小于 65536。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:296
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We also need group entries.  They are as configurable as user entries, but "
"we will use the defaults below:"
msgstr "我们还需要组条目。组条目与用户条目一样可以配置，但本例将使用以下默认设置："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:303
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dn: ou=groups,dc=example,dc=org\n"
"objectClass: top\n"
"objectClass: organizationalUnit\n"
"ou: groups\n"
msgstr "dn: ou=groups,dc=example,dc=org\nobjectClass: top\nobjectClass: organizationalUnit\nou: groups\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:309
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dn: cn=tuser,ou=groups,dc=example,dc=org\n"
"objectClass: posixGroup\n"
"objectClass: top\n"
"gidNumber: 10000\n"
"cn: tuser\n"
msgstr "dn: cn=tuser,ou=groups,dc=example,dc=org\nobjectClass: posixGroup\nobjectClass: top\ngidNumber: 10000\ncn: tuser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:313
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To enter these into your database, you can use `slapadd` or `ldapadd` on a "
"file containing these entries.  Alternatively, you can use package:sysutils/"
"ldapvi[]."
msgstr "要将这些条目添加到数据库中，可以使用 `slapadd` 或 `ldapadd` 处理包含这些条目的文件。也可以使用 package:sysutils/ldapvi[]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:316
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `ldapsearch` utility on the client machine should now return these "
"entries.  If it does, your database is properly configured to be used as an "
"LDAP authentication server."
msgstr "现在，客户端计算机上的 `ldapsearch` 工具应该能够返回这些条目。如果可以，说明数据库已正确配置，可用作 LDAP 身份验证服务器。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:318
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Client Configuration"
msgstr "客户端配置"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:322
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The client should already have OpenLDAP libraries from crossref:ldap-"
"auth[ldap-connect-client,Configuring the Client], but if you are installing "
"several client machines you will need to install package:net/openldap26-"
"client[] on each of them."
msgstr "客户端应已按照 crossref:ldap-auth[ldap-connect-client,Configuring the Client] 中的说明安装 OpenLDAP 库；但如果要安装多台客户端计算机，则需要在每台计算机上安装 package:net/openldap26-client[]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:324
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD requires two ports to be installed to authenticate against an LDAP "
"server, package:security/pam_ldap[] and package:net/nss_ldap[]."
msgstr "FreeBSD 需要安装两个 port 才能通过 LDAP 服务器进行身份验证：package:security/pam_ldap[] 和 package:net/nss_ldap[]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:326
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr "认证"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:329
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"package:security/pam_ldap[] is configured via [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/"
"ldap.conf#."
msgstr "package:security/pam_ldap[] 通过 [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/ldap.conf# 配置。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:334
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This is a _different file_ than the OpenLDAP library functions' "
"configuration file, [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/openldap/ldap.conf#; however, "
"it takes many of the same options; in fact it is a superset of that file.  "
"For the rest of this section, references to [.filename]#ldap.conf# will mean "
"[.filename]#/usr/local/etc/ldap.conf#."
msgstr "这是与 OpenLDAP 库函数的配置文件 [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/openldap/ldap.conf#__不同的文件__；不过，它支持许多相同的选项，事实上，它是该文件的超集。本节后续提到的 [.filename]#ldap.conf# 均指 [.filename]#/usr/local/etc/ldap.conf#。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:338
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Thus, we will want to copy all of our original configuration parameters from "
"[.filename]#openldap/ldap.conf# to the new [.filename]#ldap.conf#.  Once "
"this is done, we want to tell package:security/pam_ldap[] what to look for "
"on the directory server."
msgstr "因此，需要将原配置文件 [.filename]#openldap/ldap.conf# 中的所有配置参数复制到新的 [.filename]#ldap.conf#。完成后，需要告知 package:security/pam_ldap[] 应在目录服务器中查找哪些内容。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:341
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We are identifying our users with the `uid` attribute.  To configure this "
"(though it is the default), set the `pam_login_attribute` directive in [."
"filename]#ldap.conf#:"
msgstr "我们使用 `uid` 属性标识用户。要配置此项（虽然它是默认值），请在 [.filename]#ldap.conf# 中设置 `pam_login_attribute` 指令："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:343
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Setting `pam_login_attribute`"
msgstr "设置 `pam_login_attribute`"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:350
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "pam_login_attribute uid\n"
msgstr "pam_login_attribute uid\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:358
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With this set, package:security/pam_ldap[] will search the entire LDAP "
"directory under `base` for the value `uid=_username_`.  If it finds one and "
"only one entry, it will attempt to bind as that user with the password it "
"was given.  If it binds correctly, then it will allow access.  Otherwise it "
"will fail."
msgstr "设置此项后，package:security/pam_ldap[] 将在 `base` 下搜索整个 LDAP 目录，查找值为 `uid=_username_` 的条目。如果恰好找到一条记录，它将尝试使用所提供的密码以该用户身份进行绑定。如果绑定成功，则允许访问；否则，验证失败。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:364
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Users whose shell is not in [.filename]#/etc/shells# will not be able to log "
"in.  This is particularly important when Bash is set as the user shell on "
"the LDAP server.  Bash is not included with a default installation of "
"FreeBSD.  When installed from a package or port, it is located at [."
"filename]#/usr/local/bin/bash#.  Verify that the path to the shell on the "
"server is set correctly:"
msgstr "登录 shell 不在 [.filename]#/etc/shells# 中的用户将无法登录。当 LDAP 服务器将 Bash 设为用户 shell 时，这一点尤其重要。FreeBSD 默认安装中不包含 Bash。通过 package 或 port 安装后，其路径为 [.filename]#/usr/local/bin/bash#。请确认服务器上的 shell 路径设置正确："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:368
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% getent passwd username\n"
msgstr "% getent passwd username\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:373
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There are two choices when the output shows `/bin/bash` in the last column.  "
"The first is to change the user's entry on the LDAP server to [.filename]#/"
"usr/local/bin/bash#.  The second option is to create a symlink on the LDAP "
"client computer so Bash is found at the correct location:"
msgstr "当最后一列显示 `/bin/bash` 时，有两种选择。第一种是在 LDAP 服务器上将用户条目改为 [.filename]#/usr/local/bin/bash#。第二种是在 LDAP 客户端计算机上创建符号链接，使 Bash 能在正确的位置找到："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:377
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# ln -s /usr/local/bin/bash /bin/bash\n"
msgstr "# ln -s /usr/local/bin/bash /bin/bash\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:381
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Make sure that [.filename]#/etc/shells# contains entries for both `/usr/"
"local/bin/bash` and `/bin/bash`.  The user will then be able to log in to "
"the system with Bash as their shell."
msgstr "确保 [.filename]#/etc/shells# 中同时包含 `/usr/local/bin/bash` 和 `/bin/bash` 的条目。这样，用户就可以使用 Bash 作为 shell 登录系统。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:383
#, no-wrap
msgid "PAM"
msgstr "PAM"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:387
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"PAM, which stands for \"Pluggable Authentication Modules\", is the method by "
"which FreeBSD authenticates most of its sessions.  To tell FreeBSD we wish "
"to use an LDAP server, we will have to add a line to the appropriate PAM "
"file."
msgstr "PAM 是“可插拔认证模块”（Pluggable Authentication Modules）的缩写，是 FreeBSD 对大多数会话进行身份验证的方式。要让 FreeBSD 使用 LDAP 服务器，我们需要在相应的 PAM 文件中添加一行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:389
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most of the time the appropriate PAM file is [.filename]#/etc/pam.d/sshd#, "
"if you want to use SSH (remember to set the relevant options in [.filename]#/"
"etc/ssh/sshd_config#, otherwise SSH will not use PAM)."
msgstr "大多数情况下，如果要使用 SSH，相应的 PAM 文件是 [.filename]#/etc/pam.d/sshd#（记得在 [.filename]#/etc/ssh/sshd_config# 中设置相关选项，否则 SSH 不会使用 PAM）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:391
#, fuzzy
msgid "To use PAM for authentication, add the line"
msgstr "要使用 PAM 进行身份验证，请添加以下行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:395
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "auth  sufficient  /usr/local/lib/pam_ldap.so  no_warn\n"
msgstr "auth  sufficient  /usr/local/lib/pam_ldap.so  no_warn\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:398
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Exactly where this line shows up in the file and which options appear in the "
"fourth column determine the exact behavior of the authentication mechanism; "
"see man:pam[d]"
msgstr "此行在文件中的确切位置以及第四列中的选项决定了身份验证机制的具体行为；请参见 man:pam[d]"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:401
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With this configuration you should be able to authenticate a user against an "
"LDAP directory.  PAM will perform a bind with your credentials, and if "
"successful will tell SSH to allow access."
msgstr "使用此配置，您应该能够通过 LDAP 目录验证用户身份。PAM 将使用您的凭据执行绑定；如果成功，则会通知 SSH 允许访问。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:405
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"However it is not a good idea to allow _every_ user in the directory into "
"_every_ client machine.  With the current configuration, all that a user "
"needs to log into a machine is an LDAP entry.  Fortunately there are a few "
"ways to restrict user access."
msgstr "不过，允许目录中的__每个__用户登录__每台__客户端计算机并不是好主意。使用当前配置，用户只需在 LDAP 中有一个条目即可登录计算机。幸运的是，有几种限制用户访问的方法。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:408
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#ldap.conf# supports a `pam_groupdn` directive; every account "
"that connects to this machine needs to be a member of the group specified "
"here.  For example, if you have"
msgstr "[.filename]#ldap.conf# 支持 `pam_groupdn` 指令；连接到此计算机的每个帐户都必须属于此处指定的组。例如，如果您有："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:412
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "pam_groupdn cn=servername,ou=accessgroups,dc=example,dc=org\n"
msgstr "pam_groupdn cn=servername,ou=accessgroups,dc=example,dc=org\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:416
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"in [.filename]#ldap.conf#, then only members of that group will be able to "
"log in.  There are a few things to bear in mind, however."
msgstr "在 [.filename]#ldap.conf# 中，那么只有该组的成员才能登录。不过，有几点需要注意。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:419
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Members of this group are specified in one or more `memberUid` attributes, "
"and each attribute must have the full distinguished name of the member.  So "
"`memberUid: someuser` will not work; it must be:"
msgstr "此组的成员通过一个或多个 `memberUid` 属性指定，并且每个属性都必须包含成员的完整可分辨名称。因此，`memberUid: someuser` 不起作用；必须写成："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:423
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "memberUid: uid=someuser,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"
msgstr "memberUid: uid=someuser,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:429
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Additionally, this directive is not checked in PAM during authentication, it "
"is checked during account management, so you will need a second line in your "
"PAM files under `account`.  This will require, in turn, _every_ user to be "
"listed in the group, which is not necessarily what we want.  To avoid "
"blocking users that are not in LDAP, you should enable the "
"`ignore_unknown_user` attribute.  Finally, you should set the "
"`ignore_authinfo_unavail` option so that you are not locked out of every "
"computer when the LDAP server is unavailable."
msgstr "此外，PAM 不会在身份验证期间检查此指令，而是在帐户管理期间检查，因此您需要在 PAM 文件的 `account` 项下再添加一行。这样一来，__每个__用户都必须列在该组中，而这未必符合我们的需要。为避免阻止不在 LDAP 中的用户，您应启用 `ignore_unknown_user` 属性。最后，您应设置 `ignore_authinfo_unavail` 选项，以免 LDAP 服务器不可用时被锁在所有计算机之外。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:431
#, fuzzy
msgid "Your [.filename]#pam.d/sshd# might then end up looking like this:"
msgstr "您的 [.filename]#pam.d/sshd# 最终可能如下所示："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:433
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Sample [.filename]#pam.d/sshd#"
msgstr "[.filename]#pam.d/sshd# 示例"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:444
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"auth            required        pam_nologin.so          no_warn\n"
"auth            sufficient      pam_opie.so             no_warn no_fake_prompts\n"
"auth            requisite       pam_opieaccess.so       no_warn allow_local\n"
"auth            sufficient      /usr/local/lib/pam_ldap.so      no_warn\n"
"auth            required        pam_unix.so             no_warn try_first_pass\n"
msgstr "auth            required        pam_nologin.so          no_warn\nauth            sufficient      pam_opie.so             no_warn no_fake_prompts\nauth            requisite       pam_opieaccess.so       no_warn allow_local\nauth            sufficient      /usr/local/lib/pam_ldap.so      no_warn\nauth            required        pam_unix.so             no_warn try_first_pass\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:447
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"account         required        pam_login_access.so\n"
"account         required        /usr/local/lib/pam_ldap.so      no_warn ignore_authinfo_unavail ignore_unknown_user\n"
msgstr "account         required        pam_login_access.so\naccount         required        /usr/local/lib/pam_ldap.so      no_warn ignore_authinfo_unavail ignore_unknown_user\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:456
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Since we are adding these lines specifically to [.filename]#pam.d/sshd#, "
"this will only have an effect on SSH sessions.  LDAP users will be unable to "
"log in at the console.  To change this behavior, examine the other files in "
"[.filename]#/etc/pam.d# and modify them accordingly."
msgstr "由于我们专门将这些行添加到 [.filename]#pam.d/sshd#，它们只会影响 SSH 会话。LDAP 用户将无法在控制台登录。要更改此行为，请检查 [.filename]#/etc/pam.d# 中的其他文件并相应地修改它们。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:459
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Name Service Switch"
msgstr "名称服务切换"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:463
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"NSS is the service that maps attributes to names.  So, for example, if a "
"file is owned by user `1001`, an application will query NSS for the name of "
"`1001`, and it might get `bob` or `ted` or whatever the user's name is."
msgstr "NSS 是将属性映射为名称的服务。例如，如果某个文件归用户 `1001` 所有，应用程序会向 NSS 查询 `1001` 对应的名称，得到的可能是 `bob`、`ted` 或该用户的其他名称。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:465
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now that our user information is kept in LDAP, we need to tell NSS to look "
"there when queried."
msgstr "现在用户信息保存在 LDAP 中，我们需要告知 NSS 在收到查询时到那里查找。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:470
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The package:net/nss_ldap[] port does this.  It uses the same configuration "
"file as package:security/pam_ldap[], and should not need any extra "
"parameters once it is installed.  Instead, what is left is simply to edit [."
"filename]#/etc/nsswitch.conf# to take advantage of the directory.  Simply "
"replace the following lines:"
msgstr "package:net/nss_ldap[] 移植软件提供了此功能。它使用与 package:security/pam_ldap[] 相同的配置文件，安装后通常无需额外参数。接下来只需编辑 [.filename]#/etc/nsswitch.conf#，以使用该目录。只需将以下几行替换为："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:475
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"group: compat\n"
"passwd: compat\n"
msgstr "group: compat\npasswd: compat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:478
msgid "with"
msgstr "替换为"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:483
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"group: files ldap\n"
"passwd: files ldap\n"
msgstr "group: files ldap\npasswd: files ldap\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:486
#, fuzzy
msgid "This will allow you to map usernames to UIDs and UIDs to usernames."
msgstr "这样就可以将用户名映射为 UID，也可以将 UID 映射为用户名。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:488
#, fuzzy
msgid "Congratulations! You should now have working LDAP authentication."
msgstr "恭喜！现在 LDAP 身份验证应该已经可以正常工作了。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:490
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr "注意事项"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:497
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, as of the time this was written FreeBSD did not support "
"changing user passwords with man:passwd[1].  As a result of this, most "
"administrators are left to implement a solution themselves.  I provide some "
"examples here.  Note that if you write your own password change script, "
"there are some security issues you should be made aware of; see crossref:"
"ldap-auth[security-passwd, Password Storage]"
msgstr "遗憾的是，在本文撰写时，FreeBSD 尚不支持使用 man:passwd[1] 更改用户密码。因此，大多数管理员只能自行实现解决方案。这里提供了一些示例。请注意，如果您编写自己的密码更改脚本，需要了解其中的一些安全问题；请参见 crossref:ldap-auth[security-passwd, Password Storage]"

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:499
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Shell Script for Changing Passwords"
msgstr "用于更改密码的 Shell 脚本"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:506
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "#!/bin/sh\n"
msgstr "#!/bin/sh\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:512
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"stty -echo\n"
"read -p \"Old Password: \" oldp; echo\n"
"read -p \"New Password: \" np1; echo\n"
"read -p \"Retype New Password: \" np2; echo\n"
"stty echo\n"
msgstr "stty -echo\nread -p \"Old Password: \" oldp; echo\nread -p \"New Password: \" np1; echo\nread -p \"Retype New Password: \" np2; echo\nstty echo\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:517
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"if [ \"$np1\" != \"$np2\" ]; then\n"
"  echo \"Passwords do not match.\"\n"
"  exit 1\n"
"fi\n"
msgstr "if [ \"$np1\" != \"$np2\" ]; then\n  echo \"Passwords do not match.\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:522
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ldappasswd -D uid=\"$USER\",ou=people,dc=example,dc=org \\\n"
"  -w \"$oldp\" \\\n"
"  -a \"$oldp\" \\\n"
"  -s \"$np1\"\n"
msgstr "ldappasswd -D uid=\"$USER\",ou=people,dc=example,dc=org \\\n  -w \"$oldp\" \\\n  -a \"$oldp\" \\\n  -s \"$np1\"\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:531
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This script does hardly any error checking, but more important it is very "
"cavalier about how it stores your passwords.  If you do anything like this, "
"at least adjust the `security.bsd.see_other_uids` sysctl value:"
msgstr "此脚本几乎不进行错误检查，更重要的是，它对密码的存储方式相当草率。如果您要采用类似做法，至少应调整 `security.bsd.see_other_uids` sysctl 值："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:535
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sysctl security.bsd.see_other_uids=0\n"
msgstr "# sysctl security.bsd.see_other_uids=0\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:542
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A more flexible (and probably more secure) approach can be used by writing a "
"custom program, or even a web interface.  The following is part of a Ruby "
"library that can change LDAP passwords.  It sees use both on the command "
"line, and on the web."
msgstr "编写自定义程序，甚至创建 Web 界面，可以采用更灵活（也可能更安全）的方法。以下是一个可更改 LDAP 密码的 Ruby 库中的部分代码。它既可在命令行中使用，也可在 Web 上使用。"

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:544
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Ruby Script for Changing Passwords"
msgstr "用于更改密码的 Ruby 脚本"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:554
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"require 'ldap'\n"
"require 'base64'\n"
"require 'digest'\n"
"require 'password' # ruby-password\n"
msgstr "require 'ldap'\nrequire 'base64'\nrequire 'digest'\nrequire 'password' # ruby-password\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:557
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ldap_server = \"ldap.example.org\"\n"
"luser = \"uid=#{ENV['USER']},ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\"\n"
msgstr "ldap_server = \"ldap.example.org\"\nluser = \"uid=#{ENV['USER']},ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\"\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:562
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# get the new password, check it, and create a salted hash from it\n"
"def get_password\n"
"  pwd1 = Password.get(\"New Password: \")\n"
"  pwd2 = Password.get(\"Retype New Password: \")\n"
msgstr "# get the new password, check it, and create a salted hash from it\ndef get_password\n  pwd1 = Password.get(\"New Password: \")\n  pwd2 = Password.get(\"Retype New Password: \")\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:565
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  raise if pwd1 != pwd2\n"
"  pwd1.check # check password strength\n"
msgstr "  raise if pwd1 != pwd2\n  pwd1.check # check password strength\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:571
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  salt = rand.to_s.gsub(/0\\./, '')\n"
"  pass = pwd1.to_s\n"
"  hash = \"{SSHA}\"+Base64.encode64(Digest::SHA1.digest(\"#{pass}#{salt}\")+salt).chomp!\n"
"  return hash\n"
"end\n"
msgstr "  salt = rand.to_s.gsub(/0\\./, '')\n  pass = pwd1.to_s\n  hash = \"{SSHA}\"+Base64.encode64(Digest::SHA1.digest(\"#{pass}#{salt}\")+salt).chomp!\n  return hash\nend\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:574
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"oldp = Password.get(\"Old Password: \")\n"
"newp = get_password\n"
msgstr "oldp = Password.get(\"Old Password: \")\nnewp = get_password\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:577
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# We'll just replace it.  That we can bind proves that we either know\n"
"# the old password or are an admin.\n"
msgstr "# We'll just replace it.  That we can bind proves that we either know\n# the old password or are an admin.\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:581
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"replace = LDAP::Mod.new(LDAP::LDAP_MOD_REPLACE | LDAP::LDAP_MOD_BVALUES,\n"
"                        \"userPassword\",\n"
"                        [newp])\n"
msgstr "replace = LDAP::Mod.new(LDAP::LDAP_MOD_REPLACE | LDAP::LDAP_MOD_BVALUES,\n                        \"userPassword\",\n                        [newp])\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:586
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"conn = LDAP::SSLConn.new(ldap_server, 389, true)\n"
"conn.set_option(LDAP::LDAP_OPT_PROTOCOL_VERSION, 3)\n"
"conn.bind(luser, oldp)\n"
"conn.modify(luser, [replace])\n"
msgstr "conn = LDAP::SSLConn.new(ldap_server, 389, true)\nconn.set_option(LDAP::LDAP_OPT_PROTOCOL_VERSION, 3)\nconn.bind(luser, oldp)\nconn.modify(luser, [replace])\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:591
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Although not guaranteed to be free of security holes (the password is kept "
"in memory, for example) this is cleaner and more flexible than a simple `sh` "
"script."
msgstr "虽然无法保证没有安全漏洞（例如，密码会保存在内存中），但与简单的 `sh` 脚本相比，这种做法更简洁、灵活。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:593
#, no-wrap
msgid "Security Considerations"
msgstr "安全注意事项"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:596
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now that your machines (and possibly other services) are authenticating "
"against your LDAP server, this server needs to be protected at least as well "
"as [.filename]#/etc/master.passwd# would be on a regular server, and "
"possibly even more so since a broken or cracked LDAP server would break "
"every client service."
msgstr "现在，您的计算机（以及可能的其他服务）都通过 LDAP 服务器进行身份验证，因此必须至少像保护普通服务器上的 [.filename]#/etc/master.passwd# 那样保护此服务器，甚至可能需要更严格的保护，因为 LDAP 服务器一旦故障或遭到入侵，所有客户端服务都会受到影响。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:599
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Remember, this section is not exhaustive.  You should continually review "
"your configuration and procedures for improvements."
msgstr "请记住，本节并未涵盖所有内容。您应持续检查配置和流程，以寻找改进之处。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:601
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Setting Attributes Read-only"
msgstr "将属性设为只读"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:605
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Several attributes in LDAP should be read-only.  If left writable by the "
"user, for example, a user could change his `uidNumber` attribute to `0` and "
"get `root` access!"
msgstr "LDAP 中有几个属性应设为只读。例如，如果用户可以写入这些属性，就可能将自己的 `uidNumber` 属性改为 `0`，从而获得 `root` 访问权限！"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:609
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To begin with, the `userPassword` attribute should not be world-readable.  "
"By default, anyone who can connect to the LDAP server can read this "
"attribute.  To disable this, put the following in [.filename]#slapd.conf#:"
msgstr "首先，`userPassword` 属性不应允许所有人读取。默认情况下，任何能够连接到 LDAP 服务器的人都可以读取此属性。要禁用此行为，请在 [.filename]#slapd.conf# 中添加以下内容："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:611
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Hide Passwords"
msgstr "隐藏密码"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:622
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:648
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"access to dn.subtree=\"ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\"\n"
"  attrs=userPassword\n"
"  by self write\n"
"  by anonymous auth\n"
"  by * none\n"
msgstr "access to dn.subtree=\"ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\"\n  attrs=userPassword\n  by self write\n  by anonymous auth\n  by * none\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:626
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:655
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"access to *\n"
"  by self write\n"
"  by * read\n"
msgstr "access to *\n  by self write\n  by * read\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:631
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This will disallow reading of the `userPassword` attribute, while still "
"allowing users to change their own passwords."
msgstr "这样可以禁止读取 `userPassword` 属性，同时仍允许用户更改自己的密码。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:635
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Additionally, you'll want to keep users from changing some of their own "
"attributes.  By default, users can change any attribute (except for those "
"which the LDAP schemas themselves deny changes), such as `uidNumber`.  To "
"close this hole, modify the above to"
msgstr "此外，您还应禁止用户更改自己的某些属性。默认情况下，用户可以更改任何属性（LDAP 架构本身禁止更改的属性除外），例如 `uidNumber`。要堵住这一漏洞，请将上述内容修改为："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:637
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Read-only Attributes"
msgstr "只读属性"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:651
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"access to attrs=homeDirectory,uidNumber,gidNumber\n"
"  by * read\n"
msgstr "access to attrs=homeDirectory,uidNumber,gidNumber\n  by * read\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:660
#, fuzzy
msgid "This will stop users from being able to masquerade as other users."
msgstr "这样可以防止用户冒充其他用户。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:662
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`root` Account Definition"
msgstr "`root` 帐户定义"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:667
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Often the `root` or manager account for the LDAP service will be defined in "
"the configuration file.  OpenLDAP supports this, for example, and it works, "
"but it can lead to trouble if [.filename]#slapd.conf# is compromised.  It "
"may be better to use this only to bootstrap yourself into LDAP, and then "
"define a `root` account there."
msgstr "通常，LDAP 服务的 `root` 或管理者帐户会在配置文件中定义。例如，OpenLDAP 支持这种做法，而且可以正常工作，但如果 [.filename]#slapd.conf# 遭到泄露，就可能引发问题。更好的做法是仅用它引导自己进入 LDAP，然后在那里定义一个 `root` 帐户。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:671
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Even better is to define accounts that have limited permissions, and omit a "
"`root` account entirely.  For example, users that can add or remove user "
"accounts are added to one group, but they cannot themselves change the "
"membership of this group.  Such a security policy would help mitigate the "
"effects of a leaked password."
msgstr "更好的做法是定义权限受限的帐户，并完全省略 `root` 帐户。例如，可以将能够添加或删除用户帐户的用户加入一个组，但不允许他们更改该组的成员身份。这样的安全策略有助于减轻密码泄露造成的影响。"

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:673
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:679
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Creating a Management Group"
msgstr "创建管理组"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:677
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Say you want your IT department to be able to change home directories for "
"users, but you do not want all of them to be able to add or remove users.  "
"The way to do this is to add a group for these admins:"
msgstr "假设您希望 IT 部门能够更改用户的主目录，但不希望所有 IT 人员都能添加或删除用户。实现方法是为这些管理员添加一个组："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:692
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dn: cn=homemanagement,dc=example,dc=org\n"
"objectClass: top\n"
"objectClass: posixGroup\n"
"cn: homemanagement\n"
"gidNumber: 121 # required for posixGroup\n"
"memberUid: uid=tuser,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"
"memberUid: uid=user2,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"
msgstr "dn: cn=homemanagement,dc=example,dc=org\nobjectClass: top\nobjectClass: posixGroup\ncn: homemanagement\ngidNumber: 121 # required for posixGroup\nmemberUid: uid=tuser,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\nmemberUid: uid=user2,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:697
#, fuzzy
msgid "And then change the permissions attributes in [.filename]#slapd.conf#:"
msgstr "然后修改 [.filename]#slapd.conf# 中的权限属性："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:699
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ACLs for a Home Directory Management Group"
msgstr "主目录管理组的 ACL"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:709
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"access to dn.subtree=\"ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\"\n"
"  attr=homeDirectory\n"
"  by dn=\"cn=homemanagement,dc=example,dc=org\"\n"
"  dnattr=memberUid write\n"
msgstr "access to dn.subtree=\"ou=people,dc=example,dc=org\"\n  attr=homeDirectory\n  by dn=\"cn=homemanagement,dc=example,dc=org\"\n  dnattr=memberUid write\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:714
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now `tuser` and `user2` can change other users' home directories."
msgstr "现在，`tuser` 和 `user2` 可以更改其他用户的主目录。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:718
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In this example we have given a subset of administrative power to certain "
"users without giving them power in other domains.  The idea is that soon no "
"single user account has the power of a `root` account, but every power root "
"had is had by at least one user.  The `root` account then becomes "
"unnecessary and can be removed."
msgstr "在此示例中，我们赋予某些用户部分管理权限，但不赋予他们其他领域的权限。我们的设想是，最终不会有任何单个用户帐户拥有 `root` 帐户的全部权限，但 `root` 曾拥有的每项权限至少会分配给一个用户。这样一来，`root` 帐户就不再必要，可以将其删除。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:720
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Password Storage"
msgstr "密码存储"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:724
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"By default OpenLDAP will store the value of the `userPassword` attribute as "
"it stores any other data: in the clear.  Most of the time it is base 64 "
"encoded, which provides enough protection to keep an honest administrator "
"from knowing your password, but little else."
msgstr "默认情况下，OpenLDAP 会像存储其他数据一样，以明文形式存储 `userPassword` 属性的值。它通常经过 Base64 编码，这足以防止诚实的管理员知道您的密码，但除此之外几乎没有保护作用。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:727
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It is a good idea, then, to store passwords in a more secure format, such as "
"SSHA (salted SHA).  This is done by whatever program you use to change "
"users' passwords."
msgstr "因此，最好以更安全的格式存储密码，例如 SSHA（加盐 SHA）。这由您用于更改用户密码的程序完成。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:732
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Useful Aids"
msgstr "实用工具"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:735
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There are a few other programs that might be useful, particularly if you "
"have many users and do not want to configure everything manually."
msgstr "还有一些其他程序可能会很有用，尤其是在用户众多且不想手动配置所有内容时。"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:738
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"package:security/pam_mkhomedir[] is a PAM module that always succeeds; its "
"purpose is to create home directories for users which do not have them.  If "
"you have dozens of client servers and hundreds of users, it is much easier "
"to use this and set up skeleton directories than to prepare every home "
"directory."
msgstr "package:security/pam_mkhomedir[] 是一个始终返回成功的 PAM 模块；它用于为尚无主目录的用户创建主目录。如果您有数十台客户端服务器和数百名用户，使用此模块并设置骨架目录，要比逐一准备每个主目录容易得多。"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:742
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"package:sysutils/ldapvi[] is a great utility for editing LDAP values in an "
"LDIF-like syntax.  The directory (or subsection of the directory) is "
"presented in the editor chosen by the `EDITOR` environment variable.  This "
"makes it easy to enable large-scale changes in the directory without having "
"to write a custom tool."
msgstr "package:sysutils/ldapvi[] 是一个非常实用的工具，可用于以类似 LDIF 的语法编辑 LDAP 值。目录（或目录的某个子部分）会显示在 `EDITOR` 环境变量指定的编辑器中。这样，无需编写自定义工具，也能轻松对目录进行大规模更改。"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:745
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"package:security/openssh-portable[] has the ability to contact an LDAP "
"server to verify SSH keys.  This is extremely nice if you have many servers "
"and do not want to copy your public keys across all of them."
msgstr "package:security/openssh-portable[] 能够联系 LDAP 服务器以验证 SSH 密钥。如果你有许多服务器，又不想在所有服务器上复制公钥，这个功能会非常方便。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:750
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "OpenSSL Certificates for LDAP"
msgstr "LDAP 的 OpenSSL 证书"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:754
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you are hosting two or more LDAP servers, you will probably not want to "
"use self-signed certificates, since each client will have to be configured "
"to work with each certificate.  While this is possible, it is not nearly as "
"simple as creating your own certificate authority, and signing your servers' "
"certificates with that."
msgstr "如果你托管两个或更多 LDAP 服务器，可能不想使用自签名证书，因为必须为每个客户端配置所有证书才能正常使用。虽然这是可行的，但远不如创建自己的证书颁发机构并用它为服务器证书签名来得简单。"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:756
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The steps here are presented as they are with very little attempt at "
"explaining what is going on-further explanation can be found in man:"
"openssl[1] and its friends."
msgstr "这里列出的步骤几乎没有解释其背后的原理；更多说明可参阅 man:openssl[1] 及相关手册。"

#. type: appendix
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:759
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To create a certificate authority, we simply need a self-signed certificate "
"and key.  The steps for this again are"
msgstr "要创建证书颁发机构，只需一个自签名证书和密钥。具体步骤如下："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:761
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Creating a Certificate"
msgstr "创建证书"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:770
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% openssl genrsa -out root.key 1024\n"
"% openssl req -new -key root.key -out root.csr\n"
"% openssl x509 -req -days 1024 -in root.csr -signkey root.key -out root.crt\n"
msgstr "% openssl genrsa -out root.key 1024\n% openssl req -new -key root.key -out root.csr\n% openssl x509 -req -days 1024 -in root.csr -signkey root.key -out root.crt\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:776
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These will be your root CA key and certificate.  You will probably want to "
"encrypt the key and store it in a cool, dry place; anyone with access to it "
"can masquerade as one of your LDAP servers."
msgstr "这些将成为你的根 CA 密钥和证书。你可能需要加密该密钥，并将其存放在阴凉干燥处；任何能够访问它的人都可以冒充你的某台 LDAP 服务器。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:779
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next, using the first two steps above create a key [.filename]#ldap-server-"
"one.key# and certificate signing request [.filename]#ldap-server-one.csr#.  "
"Once you sign the signing request with [.filename]#root.key#, you will be "
"able to use [.filename]#ldap-server-one.*# on your LDAP servers."
msgstr "接下来，使用上面前两个步骤创建密钥 [.filename]#ldap-server-one.key# 和证书签名请求 [.filename]#ldap-server-one.csr#。使用 [.filename]#root.key# 为该签名请求签名后，就可以在 LDAP 服务器上使用 [.filename]#ldap-server-one.*#。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:783
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Do not forget to use the fully qualified domain name for the \"common name\" "
"attribute when generating the certificate signing request; otherwise clients "
"will reject a connection with you, and it can be very tricky to diagnose."
msgstr "生成证书签名请求时，别忘了在“common name”属性中使用完全限定域名；否则客户端会拒绝与你建立连接，而且问题可能很难诊断。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:786
#, fuzzy
msgid "To sign the key, use `-CA` and `-CAkey` instead of `-signkey`:"
msgstr "要为密钥签名，请使用 `-CA` 和 `-CAkey`，而不是 `-signkey`："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:788
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Signing as a Certificate Authority"
msgstr "以证书颁发机构身份签名"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:797
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% openssl x509 -req -days 1024 \\\n"
"-in ldap-server-one.csr -CA root.crt -CAkey root.key \\\n"
"-out ldap-server-one.crt\n"
msgstr "% openssl x509 -req -days 1024 \\\n-in ldap-server-one.csr -CA root.crt -CAkey root.key \\\n-out ldap-server-one.crt\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:802
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The resulting file will be the certificate that you can use on your LDAP "
"servers."
msgstr "生成的文件就是可用于 LDAP 服务器的证书。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/ldap-auth/_index.adoc:803
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Finally, for clients to trust all your servers, distribute [.filename]#root."
"crt# (the __certificate__, not the key!) to each client, and specify it in "
"the `TLSCACertificateFile` directive in [.filename]#ldap.conf#."
msgstr "最后，要让客户端信任所有服务器，请将 [.filename]#root.crt#（即__证书__，不是密钥！）分发给每个客户端，并在 [.filename]#ldap.conf# 的 `TLSCACertificateFile` 指令中指定它。"
